@startuml window_memory_save
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' window_memory_save — the SAVE half of v23/v23.1.
'
' Split out of window_memory_restore during the v26.8 audit. The Mermaid
' original drew restore and save in one flowchart with two disconnected
' entry points, which PlantUML activity syntax cannot express and which was
' confusing anyway: they are two independent stories that happen to share a
' preference key.
'
' v23.1's real change: closeEvent was demoted from "the" save to "the last"
' save. The debounce is load-bearing now because it works no matter how the
' process dies — Stop button, crash, kill — which closeEvent never did.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

title The window's memory — the save side (v23.1: the debounce is the real path)

start
:moveEvent, resizeEvent, or a
WindowStateChange changeEvent;

if (m_windowStateRestored\n&& isVisible()\n&& !isMinimized()?) then (no — construction or\nrestore in progress)
  :<b>drop</b>
  saving now would erase the
  memory with the default;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:restart a 1s single-shot QTimer;
note right
  start() on an ALREADY-RUNNING QTimer
  restarts it. That one fact <i>is</i> the
  debounce — no counter, no flag.
end note

:1s of silence elapses;

:prefs::setSidebarVisible(...)
(belt-and-braces: already written on
every Ctrl+B / toggle click);

if (isCompactScreen()?) then (yes)
  :skip — never store a
  phone-shaped rectangle;
  stop
else (no)
  :prefs::setWindowGeometry(saveGeometry());
  stop
endif

@enduml
